WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.992 --> 00:00:04.464
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.760
My name is Robert Lepage,
and I'm a stage director.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.000
But I'm also an actor, and
sometimes I'm a film director.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.710
I do a lot of work in the opera.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.190
And so I'm pretty much have
my finger in many, many pies.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.560
But my main thing
is I have a theater

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.910
company called Ex Machina.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.517
We're based in Quebec City.

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:29.100
What I thought that
this morning would

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.630
be maybe interesting to explain
to you, my method of working.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.180
It's more fun to tell
stories as a group.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.840
And it's more fun and richer
to take everybody's experience

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.960
and disciplines and make
them converge together.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.930
You help the piece say what
it is that it wants to say.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.550
So it's not starting
with that idea.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.160
It's letting it appear
and imposing itself.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.960
If you look at the anthropology
of theater, it's about playing.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.500
And that'll bring us
to our resource today.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.540
Ex Machina is working on a new
piece based on playing cards.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.420
The project is
called Playing Cards.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.890
We believe that the content
is in here, that there's

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:14.240
tons of stories in this.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.270
And I believe that if we
give you that resource

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.086
that you actually can come up
with your own interpretation.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.680
My mom used to play poker
every night when I was a kid.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.540
So I see cards and I have
flashbacks immediately.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.524
So it's a family thing.

00:01:33.524 --> 00:01:38.700
It was a family issue for sure.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.080
Yeah.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.040
When I was talking about
the way we explore this.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.120
And at least one thing we
could try this afternoon

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.620
in the playfulness
of this is we try

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.900
to play cards, just play cards.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.560
Just do that.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.432
OK, I get it.

00:01:53.432 --> 00:01:55.820
[CHATTER]

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.560
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.703
Do it, do it, do
it, do it, do it.

00:02:01.703 --> 00:02:02.245
Embarrassing.

00:02:02.245 --> 00:02:03.235
[INAUDIBLE]

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:06.154
Because I can't defend
anything else but [INAUDIBLE]

00:02:06.154 --> 00:02:08.133
[CHATTER]

00:02:17.023 --> 00:02:18.940
You can throw it down
at any time and be like,

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.332
it's now a hearts or
it's now a diamonds.

00:02:21.332 --> 00:02:23.290
And the object is to get
rid of all your cards.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.360
Are there any cards
that have special--

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:25.930
Just eights.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:26.780
Just eights.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.790
OK.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.052
[CHATTER]

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.918
Anyone else want to--

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.680
OK, all games are over.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.360
All right.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.728
So the last thing I want
us to take some time to do,

00:02:47.728 --> 00:02:49.270
which is something
I always try to do

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.130
as part of the
exploration thing,

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.958
is that we'll just do one
big collective drawing.

00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:55.000
There's no rules to this.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.640
You just draw the
impressions that you

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.560
have of what we did together
today about cards, whatever.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.941
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.550
We're just going to
quickly go around,

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.650
everyone, just to know
what who contributed what.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.630
What about you?

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.080
I had at the axe to the
players at the main table.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.015
Oh this axe here.

00:03:23.015 --> 00:03:23.640
That's the axe.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.380
OK.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.890
I did the outline of this
purple figure, the train

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.310
that people turn into a train.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.690
What's that outline?

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:38.250
So it's as you go left to
right, it's the number of cards

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.410
that you need for
the hand in poker.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:43.760
So it's one card, one pair,
two pair, three of a kind.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.200
It's an interesting pattern.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.040
I added the mustache.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:48.540
Aha.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.330
We found the culprit.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.520
Sorry.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.550
With experience, we've
learned that we should not

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.800
force connections.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:58.460
We let them.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.950
And eventually two or three
things seems to go together.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.690
And we go, oh, there's
a pattern there.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.480
And then we sit and we
score, which is of course

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.700
is a weird way of
thinking because we're

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.060
used what we were brought up
to say, you're the master.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:11.900
You're the writer.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.840
You're the guy who
controls the show, who

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.310
says to the show what to do.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:16.850
We say, no.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.480
It's exactly the opposite.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.635
We trust that the show
will tell us what to do.

00:04:21.635 --> 00:04:23.240
It's an obscure process.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.830
I agree.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.930
Any questions?

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.945
Any doubts?

00:04:27.945 --> 00:04:28.445
Any fears?

00:04:31.002 --> 00:04:32.210
So good luck with everything.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.610
And have fun.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.050
That's the most important thing.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.610
Have fun and be playful.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.140
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.040
Thank you.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.240
[INAUDIBLE]

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.290
[MUSIC PLAYING]

